### Mirrored EN/ZH pairing (`i18n-en-zh`)

Every authored English Markdown file `foo.md` pairs with `foo.zh.md` and a sibling sidecar `foo.i18n.yaml`:

```yaml
source: foo.md
target: foo.zh.md
source_sha256: <64-hex-sha256-of-foo.md>
```

- Update `foo.md` and `foo.zh.md` in the same change so meaning stays synchronized without forcing awkward literal line-count parity.
- Refresh `source_sha256` only after semantically updating the counterpart (`BD060` fails when `foo.md` changes without updating `foo.i18n.yaml`).
- Code fences, CLI commands, and identifiers stay identical across both files.
